#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# association_map

#% text
# `association_map(f, xs)` gives the association of the entries `x -> f(x)` for the elements of the list `xs` (a repeated element once). For an association `a`, it applies `f` to each rule `k -> v` and builds the association of the results. `association_map(f)` is the operator form, `association_map(f)(xs)` being `association_map(f, xs)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
association_map(f, [a, b, c])
#% output
#= assoc(a -> f(a), b -> f(b), c -> f(c))

#% cell
association_map(x => x^2, range(5))
#% output
#= assoc(1 -> 1, 2 -> 4, 3 -> 9, 4 -> 16, 5 -> 25)

#% cell
association_map(reverse, assoc(a -> 1, b -> 2))
#% output
#= assoc(1 -> a, 2 -> b)

